{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XAEmzGo24H72QaohBL6EcS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Experiment 7 Distinction-Inference Protocol v2 — Session D-E7\n2\t\n3\tYou are **D-E7**, a decision-support session in a fresh, governed workspace\n4\tunder `contract.json`. Your workspace contains a raw task package. Your job\n5\tis **stage S1 of a topology pipeline**: infer, from raw task semantics\n6\talone, which unresolved distinctions matter, type the evidence relation each\n7\tdistinction requires, and estimate the epistemic value of resolving each\n8\tdistinction. You do **not** solve the task and you do **not** select a\n9\ttopology — selection is performed later by a deterministic ranker outside\n10\tyour session.\n11\t\n12\tNothing outside this workspace is readable or writable. Your session grants\n13\tonly the tools **Read** and **Write**. You must not attempt to launch any\n14\tprocess, session, or agent.\n15\t\n16\t## Workspace layout\n17\t\n18\t```text\n19\tpackage/task.json                  the task: statement, deliverable spec, evidence requirements\n20\tpackage/artifacts/...              all task materials\n21\tcontract.json                      governing contract\n22\tinfer-harness.json                 your declared HarnessSpec (4 nodes, linear)\n23\tdistinction-spec-schema.json       required shape of distinctions.json (v2)\n24\tvalue-estimates-schema.json        required shape of value-estimates.json (v2)\n25\tprotocol.md                        this file\n26\t```\n27\t\n28\t## What you produce\n29\t\n30\t### 1. `distinctions.json` (DistinctionSpec v2)\n31\t\n32\tSame structure and honesty rules as the base DistinctionSpec: 1–8\n33\tdistinctions, ids Q1, Q2, …, each with `question`, `why_unresolved`,\n34\t`required_evidence`, `admissibility_constraints`,\n35\t`evidence_requirement_refs` (every task evidence requirement referenced at\n36\tleast once), `dependencies`, and `features`.\n37\t\n38\t`features` now has **nine** required booleans. The five base features:\n39\t\n40\t- `locally_resolvable`: this session-shaped process, having read the\n41\t  package, could produce admissible evidence settling this distinction by\n42\t  itself.\n43\t- `requires_isolation`: admissible evidence requires an origin causally\n44\t  separated from this process.\n45\t- `contamination`: reading the package has already destroyed this process's\n46\t  ability to produce that admissible evidence.\n47\t- `capability_bearing_artifact`: resolving this distinction requires\n48\t  authoring an artifact that grants execution capability.\n49\t- `spans_sessions`: resolution inherently spans process/session boundaries.\n50\t\n51\tAnd four **typed relation features** — the heart of this stage. Each names a\n52\t*distinct* epistemic relation; they are not degrees of one scale, and at\n53\tmost one of them should be true for a given distinction (set it only when\n54\tthe task's own admissibility conditions require that specific relation):\n55\t\n56\t- `requires_clean_room_authorship`: the admissible evidence must be\n57\t  *authored* by a process that never had access to a contaminating\n58\t  artifact (e.g. an implementation written solely from a description,\n59\t  where reading the reference voids authorship). Review of contaminated\n60\t  work cannot satisfy this.\n61\t- `requires_nonauthor_search`: the admissible evidence is a *search or\n62\t  examination* (e.g. hunting for a violating input) that must be performed\n63\t  by a party that did not author the candidate answer. The searcher may\n64\t  see the answer; it must not be its author.\n65\t- `requires_independent_decomposition`: the admissible evidence is a\n66\t  *second enumeration/decomposition* produced without access to the first;\n67\t  re-checking the first enumeration cannot satisfy this.\n68\t- `requires_method_disjoint_verification`: the admissible evidence is a\n69\t  *re-derivation through a different method* than the one that produced\n70\t  the answer; a same-method re-check cannot satisfy this, regardless of\n71\t  who performs it.\n72\t\n73\tA distinction with none of the four typed features true is one whose\n74\tadmissible evidence this process's own work can supply (with deterministic\n75\troot verification). Judge from the task's own evidence requirements and\n76\tadmissibility conditions; most distinctions in most tasks have all four\n77\tfalse.\n78\t\n79\t### 2. `value-estimates.json` (v2)\n80\t\n81\tPer-distinction value estimates:\n82\t\n83\t```json\n84\t{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"estimates\": {\"Q1\": {\"value\": 0.8, \"rationale\": \"...\"},\n85\t                                 \"Q2\": {\"value\": 0.5, \"rationale\": \"...\"}}}\n86\t```\n87\t\n88\t`value` in [0,1]: the relative weight of resolving this distinction with\n89\tadmissible evidence, measured as its share of the task's\n90\t`evidence_requirements` (a distinction mapping to more/harder requirements\n91\tcarries more value). These estimates feed a deterministic saturating\n92\tutility: coverage of a required relation earns the distinction's value\n93\tonce; extra structure earns nothing. `rationale`: one or two sentences.\n94\t\n95\tCosts, redundancy, and governance risk are **not** estimated in v2: they\n96\tare computed deterministically from candidate structure.\n97\t\n98\t## Ledger\n99\t\n100\tMaintain `execution-ledger.jsonl` exactly as in the base protocol: five\n101\tnode events in order (observe-package, infer-distinctions, estimate-value,\n102\tself-check-spec, return-spec), each with `metadata.completes_node`; JSON\n103\tdeliverable authoring events use label `propose`.\n104\t\n105\t## Conduct\n106\t\n107\t1. `observe-package`: read everything in the workspace.\n108\t2. `infer-distinctions`: write `distinctions.json`.\n109\t3. `estimate-value`: write `value-estimates.json`.\n110\t4. `self-check-spec`: re-read both artifacts against their schemas; record\n111\t   the outcome in the ledger (non-authoritative).\n112\t5. `return-spec`: write `spec-summary.json` — `{\"task_id\": ...,\n113\t   \"distinction_count\": N, \"typed_features\": true}` — and finish the\n114\t   ledger. Do not emit a `complete` event.\n115\t\n116\tHonesty over confidence: your distinctions, typed relations, and estimates\n117\tare scored against what later actually happens, not against how thorough\n118\tthey look.\n119\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2f5fa04-370b-4912-8158-e24cdf5f0710","uuid":"2f5c8510-f0d2-4a45-842f-3b67943a1e40","timestamp":"2026-08-09T20:42:30.039Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/87cd2a2d-a4f9-585b-836f-2648df7a6284/scratchpad/e7run/B/e7-t02/infer-ws/protocol.md","content":"# Experiment 7 Distinction-Inference Protocol v2 — Session D-E7\n\nYou are **D-E7**, a decision-support session in a fresh, governed workspace\nunder `contract.json`. Your workspace contains a raw task package. Your job\nis **stage S1 of a topology pipeline**: infer, from raw task semantics\nalone, which unresolved distinctions matter, type the evidence relation each\ndistinction requires, and estimate the epistemic value of resolving each\ndistinction. You do **not** solve the task and you do **not** select a\ntopology — selection is performed later by a deterministic ranker outside\nyour session.\n\nNothing outside this workspace is readable or writable. Your session grants\nonly the tools **Read** and **Write**. You must not attempt to launch any\nprocess, session, or agent.\n\n## Workspace layout\n\n```text\npackage/task.json                  the task: statement, deliverable spec, evidence requirements\npackage/artifacts/...              all task materials\ncontract.json                      governing contract\ninfer-harness.json                 your declared HarnessSpec (4 nodes, linear)\ndistinction-spec-schema.json       required shape of distinctions.json (v2)\nvalue-estimates-schema.json        required shape of value-estimates.json (v2)\nprotocol.md                        this file\n```\n\n## What you produce\n\n### 1. `distinctions.json` (DistinctionSpec v2)\n\nSame structure and honesty rules as the base DistinctionSpec: 1–8\ndistinctions, ids Q1, Q2, …, each with `question`, `why_unresolved`,\n`required_evidence`, `admissibility_constraints`,\n`evidence_requirement_refs` (every task evidence requirement referenced at\nleast once), `dependencies`, and `features`.\n\n`features` now has **nine** required booleans. The five base features:\n\n- `locally_resolvable`: this session-shaped process, having read the\n  package, could produce admissible evidence settling this distinction by\n  itself.\n- `requires_isolation`: admissible evidence requires an origin causally\n  separated from this process.\n- `contamination`: reading the package has already destroyed this process's\n  ability to produce that admissible evidence.\n- `capability_bearing_artifact`: resolving this distinction requires\n  authoring an artifact that grants execution capability.\n- `spans_sessions`: resolution inherently spans process/session boundaries.\n\nAnd four **typed relation features** — the heart of this stage. Each names a\n*distinct* epistemic relation; they are not degrees of one scale, and at\nmost one of them should be true for a given distinction (set it only when\nthe task's own admissibility conditions require that specific relation):\n\n- `requires_clean_room_authorship`: the admissible evidence must be\n  *authored* by a process that never had access to a contaminating\n  artifact (e.g. an implementation written solely from a description,\n  where reading the reference voids authorship). Review of contaminated\n  work cannot satisfy this.\n- `requires_nonauthor_search`: the admissible evidence is a *search or\n  examination* (e.g. hunting for a violating input) that must be performed\n  by a party that did not author the candidate answer. The searcher may\n  see the answer; it must not be its author.\n- `requires_independent_decomposition`: the admissible evidence is a\n  *second enumeration/decomposition* produced without access to the first;\n  re-checking the first enumeration cannot satisfy this.\n- `requires_method_disjoint_verification`: the admissible evidence is a\n  *re-derivation through a different method* than the one that produced\n  the answer; a same-method re-check cannot satisfy this, regardless of\n  who performs it.\n\nA distinction with none of the four typed features true is one whose\nadmissible evidence this process's own work can supply (with deterministic\nroot verification). Judge from the task's own evidence requirements and\nadmissibility conditions; most distinctions in most tasks have all four\nfalse.\n\n### 2. `value-estimates.json` (v2)\n\nPer-distinction value estimates:\n\n```json\n{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"estimates\": {\"Q1\": {\"value\": 0.8, \"rationale\": \"...\"},\n                                 \"Q2\": {\"value\": 0.5, \"rationale\": \"...\"}}}\n```\n\n`value` in [0,1]: the relative weight of resolving this distinction with\nadmissible evidence, measured as its share of the task's\n`evidence_requirements` (a distinction mapping to more/harder requirements\ncarries more value). These estimates feed a deterministic saturating\nutility: coverage of a required relation earns the distinction's value\nonce; extra structure earns nothing. `rationale`: one or two sentences.\n\nCosts, redundancy, and governance risk are **not** estimated in v2: they\nare computed deterministically from candidate structure.\n\n## Ledger\n\nMaintain `execution-ledger.jsonl` exactly as in the base protocol: five\nnode events in order (observe-package, infer-distinctions, estimate-value,\nself-check-spec, return-spec), each with `metadata.completes_node`; JSON\ndeliverable authoring events use label `propose`.\n\n## Conduct\n\n1. `observe-package`: read everything in the workspace.\n2. `infer-distinctions`: write `distinctions.json`.\n3. `estimate-value`: write `value-estimates.json`.\n4. `self-check-spec`: re-read both artifacts against their schemas; record\n   the outcome in the ledger (non-authoritative).\n5. `return-spec`: write `spec-summary.json` — `{\"task_id\": ...,\n   \"distinction_count\": N, \"typed_features\": true}` — and finish the\n   ledger. Do not emit a `complete` event.\n\nHonesty over confidence: your distinctions, typed relations, and estimates\nare scored against what later actually happens, not against how thorough\nthey look.\n","numLines":119,"startLine":1,"totalLines":119}}}
